    "title": "Canton police will be 'strictly' enforcing juvenile curfew for HOF festivities - NewsBreak",
    "text": "CANTON ‒ Under 18? Don't plan on hanging out late at night unsupervised for the Pro Football Hall of Fame Enshrinement Festival or First Friday activities. Canton police issued a statement July 30 saying the city's juvenile curfew will be strictly enforced, specifically citing the Grand Parade route and the First Friday event downtown on the night of Aug. 1. It's tradition for people to claim their spots and sometimes camp out overnight for a good parade spot. The city imposes restrictions for minors being out and about from 11 p.m. to 6 a.m. The curfew begins earlier — at 9 p.m. — in the designated outdoor refreshment areas (DORAs), which cover much of downtown and the Hall of Fame Village. \"These areas will have a significant law enforcement presence and the parents/guardians of unsupervised juveniles on the parade route contacted after 11 p.m. will be subject to citations,\" Police Chief John Gabbard said in a news release. Minors are exempt from the curfew if they are accompanied by a parent or guardian or if they are traveling for work, certain organized activities and emergencies. \"This enforcement and other measures are designed for the safety of our children and the reduction of disruptions that detract from what are overwhelmingly safe and enjoyable community events,\" the release said. This article originally appeared on The Repository: Canton police will be 'strictly' enforcing juvenile curfew for HOF festivities",
